Title: Magnetic button: click when the Enter release was already dispatched
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: With the focus elsewhere (Save/Open file name field), Enter is caught by the focus-magnet OK button, which moves the focus and calls Manager::dispatchMessages() before setSelected(true). When the key release is already queued (key press and release in one event batch, as on a busy or slow system), that nested dispatch delivers the key-up to the old focus first; the button stays selected and never clicks, so Enter does not confirm the dialog.
Change: After setSelected(true), if the key is no longer pressed (she::is_key_pressed), the button generates its select signal at once.
Scope: all platforms (ui library)
Upstream: candidate
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16: Enter in Save (RAM:enter1.png), keypad Enter in Save As (RAM:keypad2.png) and Enter in Open (RAM:enter1.png) all confirm; Enter in New Sprite still works; typed names arrive complete. Diagnosed with a temporary log in Widget::sendMessage: the Enter key-up was consumed by the file name ComboBoxEntry inside the OK button key-down handler
Removal: when upstream fixes the magnet path.
---
diff --git a/src/ui/button.cpp b/src/ui/button.cpp
index f2433bea7c79952cf48a5e688dcfda7caa9822a1..46cb0ad38611d6f3faa0352624b97fc6ace1d29e 100644
--- a/src/ui/button.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/button.cpp
@@ -134,6 +134,12 @@ bool ButtonBase::onProcessMessage(Message* msg)
             manager()->dispatchMessages();
 
             setSelected(true);
+
+            // That dispatch may already have delivered the key-up of
+            // this key (both arrive together on a busy system), so
+            // the button would wait for a release that never comes.
+            if (!she::is_key_pressed(scancode))
+              generateButtonSelectSignal();
             return true;
           }
         }
